lifeos-nix patch f4-c — privacy: disable default-on external-egress in base PULSE.toml

PROBLEM
  Klemen's north-star for lifeos-nix is privacy-by-construction: the shipped tree must
  not phone out to any non-Anthropic endpoint on its own. 7.40.4's base PULSE.toml ships
  several egress vectors default-ON. Regenerated against 7.40.4 (was 7.1.1); the module
  model changed (new [modules] map + legacy [section].enabled which still WINS).

  Killed here (all confirmed external egress):
    - [voice] + [modules] voice   — cloud TTS (elevenlabs HTTP already hard-killed in f4-b;
                                     the surface/module is turned off too, defense-in-depth)
    - [local_intelligence] + [modules] local — civic-digest fetch to an external service
    - [notifications.ntfy]        — ntfy.sh (external)
    - [notifications.discord]     — Discord webhook (external)
    - [notifications.twilio]      — Twilio SMS (external)
    - [notifications.routing]     — long_task/background_agent/error/security → [] (no
                                     routing to the now-dead external channels)
    - [[job]] healthcheck output "ntfy" → "log" (no egress to a disabled channel)

  DELIBERATELY KEPT ENABLED (local-only in 7.40.4, zero egress → no privacy reason to cut;
  DIVERGES from the old 7.1.1 f4-c, correctly, because upstream changed them):
    - memory-consolidation  — type="script", SessionHarvester + LearningPatternSynthesis,
                              deterministic, no LLM, no network (was claude-type in 7.1.1).
    - life-morning-brief    — reads local TELOS files only, output="log", no fetch.

  OBSOLETE vs the old f4-c (upstream removed/moved → not re-ported):
    - telegram module        — deleted entirely in 7.40.4 (also handled in f4-b note).
    - airgradient-poll       — moved to LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/PULSE.user.toml upstream.

DECISION PROVENANCE
  Klemen, 2026-08-27 (7.40.4 migration): "ubij vse tri [ntfy/discord/twilio]" +
  "patch base PULSE.toml (privacy-by-construction)". The derivation itself is privacy-hard,
  not dependent on a user-config override that could be forgotten.

VERIFICATION
  Post-build: `grep -nE 'enabled = true' PULSE.toml` shows no external-egress section on;
  egress-test (deny-all netns) stays ∅-external. Hunks via `git diff`, never hand-counted.

diff --git a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml
index e2df9ee..2772eea 100644
--- a/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml
+++ b/LifeOS/install/LIFEOS/PULSE/PULSE.toml
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ health = true
 finances = true
 business = true
 growth = true       # audience metrics; needs USER/CUSTOMIZATIONS/TOOLS/Growth.ts
-local = true        # LocalIntelligence civic digest; needs a Hometown set
+local = false       # lifeos-nix: LocalIntelligence civic digest fetches externally (egress) → off
 gear = true
 atlas = true
 memory = true
@@ -56,13 +56,13 @@ docs = true
 # the default. voice defaults on; imessage, syslog, and da default off. Turn
 # syslog on only after wiring a router/firewall to the [syslog] listener below;
 # turn da on once a DA identity is configured (its heartbeat spawns agents).
-voice = true
+voice = false       # lifeos-nix: voice surface off (cloud TTS egress killed in f4-b)
 imessage = false
 syslog = false
 da = false
 
 [voice]
-enabled = true
+enabled = false  # lifeos-nix: no cloud voice egress (privacy)
 
 [imessage]
 enabled = false
@@ -76,16 +76,16 @@ port = 31337
 enabled = true
 
 [notifications.ntfy]
-enabled = true
+enabled = false  # lifeos-nix: ntfy.sh is external egress (privacy)
 topic = "${NTFY_TOPIC}"
 server = "ntfy.sh"
 
 [notifications.discord]
-enabled = true
+enabled = false  # lifeos-nix: external Discord webhook egress (privacy)
 webhook = "${DISCORD_WEBHOOK}"
 
 [notifications.twilio]
-enabled = true
+enabled = false  # lifeos-nix: external Twilio SMS egress (privacy)
 to_number = "${TWILIO_TO_NUMBER}"
 
 [notifications.thresholds]
@@ -93,10 +93,10 @@ long_task_minutes = 5
 
 [notifications.routing]
 task_complete = []
-long_task = ["ntfy"]
-background_agent = ["ntfy"]
-error = ["ntfy", "discord"]
-security = ["ntfy", "discord"]
+long_task = []      # lifeos-nix: no external notification routing (privacy)
+background_agent = []
+error = []
+security = []
 
 [performance]
 enabled = true
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ name = "healthcheck"
 schedule = "*/5 * * * *"
 type = "script"
 command = "bun run checks/health.ts"
-output = "ntfy"
+output = "log"  # lifeos-nix: no ntfy egress (privacy)
 enabled = true
 
 # NOTE: cost-tracker moved to LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/PULSE.user.toml on 2026-05-03 —
